RouterModule – NestJS (Notes)

1. What is RouterModule?
RouterModule is used to organize routes using modules
Helps create module-based routing
Useful for large applications
👉 It allows you to define route prefixes for modules.

2. Why use RouterModule?
Clean URL structure
Better module separation
Easy to manage large apps
Improves readability and maintenance

3. Importing RouterModule
import { RouterModule } from '@nestjs/core';


4. Basic Usage Example
AppModule (Root Routing)
// app.module.ts
import { Module } from '@nestjs/common';
import { RouterModule } from '@nestjs/core';
import { UserModule } from './user/user.module';
import { AdminModule } from './admin/admin.module';

@Module({
  imports: [
    UserModule,
    AdminModule,
    RouterModule.register([
      { path: 'users', module: UserModule },
      { path: 'admin', module: AdminModule },
    ]),
  ],
})
export class AppModule {}


