6. Feature Module Example
// user.controller.ts
@Controller()
export class UserController {
  @Get('profile')
  getProfile() {
    return 'User Profile';
  }
}

Final route:
/users/profile


7. Nested Routes (Child Routes)
RouterModule.register([
  {
    path: 'admin',
    module: AdminModule,
    children: [
      { path: 'users', module: UserModule },
    ],
  },
]);

Final route:
/admin/users


8. Key Points
Works at module level
Controllers do NOT need route prefixes
Supports nested routing
Best for large-scale applications

9. RouterModule vs @Controller Prefix
RouterModule
@Controller('path')
Module-based
Controller-based
Centralized routing
Distributed routing
Better for big apps
Good for small apps


